# What EAS Build uploads. Read the next paragraph before editing.
#
# EAS archives from the GIT ROOT, not from mobile/, so building the phone app
# otherwise ships the entire monorepo - backend, web, docs - to Expo's servers.
#
# **THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore FOR EAS.** When .easignore exists, EAS stops
# consulting .gitignore entirely, so every secret rule below has to be restated
# here. Leave out the .env lines and backend/.env - holding JWT_SECRET,
# FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY, EMAIL_PASS and ORS_API_KEY - is uploaded to a third
# party's build machine. Anything added to .gitignore must be added here too.

# ── Secrets: NEVER upload ──────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
gcs-key.json
**/gcs-key.json
*.jks
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# ── Not needed to build the phone app ──────────────────────
# Mobile is a self-contained Expo app; it cannot import from web/ or backend/
# (see mobile/AGENTS.md), so none of this belongs in the build context.
backend/
web/
docs/
scripts/
testsprite-plans/
.github/

# ── Agent/editor tooling ───────────────────────────────────
# .agents/skills/ contains SYMLINKS into .claude/skills/. Recreating a symlink
# during the upload needs admin rights or Developer Mode on Windows, so the
# build fails with "EPERM: operation not permitted, symlink" before it starts.
# Nothing here is part of the app.
.agents/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.hallmark/
.playwright-mcp/
.mcp.json
skills-lock.json

# ── Dependencies and build output ──────────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
build/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/generated/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/.expo-shared/

# ── Local noise ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*.orig.*
